  "title": "Re-normalize / Edit with AI: fold busy and error into the phase, guard stale accepts",
  "description": "Web ProposalJobModal.tsx: Phase is a union (62-67) but busy and error sit outside it (86-87) and mean different things in choose (starting) and review (accepting). accept (205-219) has no session guard and calls props.onClose() even if the modal was closed and reopened. \
Opening in edit mode doesn't reset ops/selected (99-131). \
Web BulkReNormalizeModal.tsx: Row is a string status plus nullable jobId/error/base/proposed (32-49), so 'ready' with proposed null is representable and the render uses row.base!/row.proposed! (376-393); 'failed' is set without an error at 148; accept (198-218) has no session check, so an accept from a previous session can set accepted after reopen reset it (94) and fire onAccepted. iOS ProposalJobSheet.swift: Phase (38-44) is bypassed by error, isBusy, jobId, proposal and steps. error and .failed both render (225-229, 301-304). \
If listOps fails, load() sets error and phase .choose with empty ops (120-123), a dead end with no retry; .failed has no way back to .choose. \
The Accept Task (388-394) isn't stored, and Discard (371-374) isn't disabled while busy, so Discard can close the sheet and the accept still saves. \
Want on both: per-phase payloads (e.g. choose(error), starting, running(jobId, steps), review(proposal, accepting, error), failed with retry) and session/generation checks on accept. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
